WEBVTT

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:01.173
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:02.047 --> 00:00:07.527
<v><b>M:</b></v> São Paulo is currently the fourth biggest city in the world in terms of population.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:10.194
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:10.987 --> 00:00:13.480
<v><b>M:</b></v> The further south you travel from São Paulo,

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.673
the more you notice the German influence in Brazil.

00:00:18.592 --> 00:00:19.520
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.578
<v><b>M:</b></v> There is a popular cliché that São Paulo is Brazil’s New York,

00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:27.832
whereas Rio de Janeiro is Los Angeles.

00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:30.567
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:36.579
<v><b>M:</b></v> The cost of living in São Paulo is almost twice as high as that of Cairo.

00:00:38.306 --> 00:00:39.228
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:00:40.126 --> 00:00:45.714
<v><b>F:</b></v> Unlike some capital cities, Cairo has an extremely efficient metro system.

00:00:47.511 --> 00:00:48.558
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:00:49.451 --> 00:00:54.647
<v><b>F:</b></v> Alexandria, Egypt’s second city, is significantly smaller than Cairo.

00:00:56.509 --> 00:00:57.435
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7

00:00:58.226 --> 00:01:03.827
<v><b>F:</b></v> Cairo is far and away the most popular tourist destination in Egypt.